From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:23:15 -0500
Subject: fix: the lit circle is the size of the chips beside it

At 20 DIP the circle behind a lit shield or moon was right in strength and a
little small. It is 21 DIP now, the size of the address field's chips on the
same row. An odd size has edges between pixels at 1x, so the bounds are a
RectF: the enclosing Rect would have painted 22.

Why: the owner's look on the Mac, 2026-11-06 (BACKLOG S-423, toolbar T60).

Removable when: fold it into the patch that made the circle, once the Mac's
series matches this one.
